[[File:Norikiyo_Live_2018.jpg|175px|thumb|upright|Rapper [[NORIKIYO]] defined the 2018 charts, securing the top spot for a combined 10 weeks with "Nihongo Rap No Joke Show" and the massive hit "Kanjosen" (Loop Line), which reigned for eight consecutive weeks in the autumn.]]

The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2018.

2018 was a watershed year for the Sanese music industry, often called the "Hip-Hop Revolution" ({{nihongo|Hip-Hop Kakumei|ヒップホップ革命}}). While veteran pop icon [[Namie Amuro]] dominated headlines with her retirement, the weekly charts were overwhelmed by domestic rap artists. **NORIKIYO**'s "Kanjosen" became the longest-running number-one hip-hop single in history at the time. This year also saw the breakthrough of **BAD HOP**, who brought the "Kawasaki Drift" sound to the mainstream, setting the stage for the drill movement of the 2020s.

